# Books folder — YOUR corpus is never committed. Only books/sample/ ships.
#
# `books/` is the corpus mount. Everything in it is your library and must stay
# local. The one exception is `books/sample/`: five public-domain works that
# ship with the repo so the first boot indexes something instead of nothing.
books/*
!books/.gitkeep
!books/sample/
books/sample/*.DS_Store

# Index / state artifacts — derived, never published (P4: no corpus state in the
# package). Rebuilt in seconds by the entrypoint on first boot.
books/*.index
books/*.db
books/book_registry.json*
books/.index_state.json*
books/.faiss_rebuild_ckpt.json
books/.global-index*
books/.index-*
books/.index-text/
books/.archive/

# Embedding model — downloaded on first boot, never committed (~128 MB).
models/
models/.locks/

# Reading state — runtime data, not committed
engine/reading_state/*
!engine/reading_state/.gitkeep

# Instance-only operational artifacts — NOT part of the publishable/generic product.
# Kept on disk (dev repo) but never tracked → never in a release candidate.
DO_NOT.md
quarantine.jsonl

# Local instance dirs (never in a release candidate)
backup/
covers/
flagship/
staging/
quarantine/
reading_log/
memory/
logs/
testing/
EPIC.md
staging/
*.bak-*
*.bak.*
log-rebuild-*.txt
log-reindex-*.log
.DS_Store
